The visual redesign must never take priority over educational accuracy.

Inspect the actual syllabus files, chapter data, curated notes, fallback generators, question banks, and AI prompts.

Identify every supported class, subject, chapter, and topic. Verify names, order, mappings, and content against the applicable official NCERT textbooks and syllabus materials.

Use the appropriate edition and account for applicable syllabus changes. Do not assume that every historical textbook chapter remains part of the current syllabus.

Create a structured content inventory that records:

- Class and subject.
- Chapter identifier and chapter title.
- Topics and subtopics.
- Whether notes exist.
- Whether the notes are complete.
- Whether the content has been verified against an appropriate source.
- Whether questions, diagrams, examples, and revision materials exist.
- Any identified errors or missing material.

Use this inventory to identify gaps systematically.

## 7.1 Correct generic fallback content

Search for generic placeholders, repeated definitions, empty explanations, unrelated examples, incorrect chapter labels, and text that gives the appearance of complete notes without teaching anything.

Replace such content with accurate, chapter-specific explanations wherever reliable source material is available.

If the correct content cannot be verified, show a clear content-unavailable or under-review message. Do not generate a random explanation just to make a chapter appear complete.

Make the fallback logic intelligent enough to distinguish between an unavailable resource and valid chapter-specific content.

## 7.2 Use AI responsibly

AI may help draft explanations, create practice questions, simplify difficult concepts, and propose diagrams. However, AI-generated content must not automatically be labelled as verified NCERT material.

Use trusted source context, the correct class and chapter, and the applicable learning objective when generating educational material.

Validate generated responses for completeness, structure, relevance, and answer consistency. Verify factual claims against authoritative sources when required.

Where source verification has not occurred, identify the material as AI-generated or unverified as appropriate.

Remove unsupported claims such as guaranteed examination questions, guaranteed results, or complete syllabus coverage unless there is adequate evidence for the claim.

Do not fabricate textbook quotations, page numbers, references, or official endorsements.

